Disable nvmath's numba-cuda backend

nvmath gates its numba-cuda backend on `find_spec("numba.cuda")`, which cannot
express "numba-cuda is absent": with no numba installed the probe raises
ModuleNotFoundError, and with plain numba installed it matches numba's own
`numba/cuda` shim and then fails importing the backend modules. This CI job
installs neither numba nor numba-cuda - it exercises only the numba-cuda-mlir
backend - so pin the gate off.

TODO: drop once nvmath-python makes the probe tolerant of a missing numba.

Applied by ci/tools/run-nvmath-python-mlir-tests.

diff --git a/nvmath/device/common.py b/nvmath/device/common.py
--- a/nvmath/device/common.py
+++ b/nvmath/device/common.py
@@ -14,7 +14,7 @@ import numpy as np

 from .common_cuda import MAX_SUPPORTED_CC, MIN_SUPPORTED_CC, CodeType, ComputeCapability, get_current_device_cc

-_HAS_NUMBA = importlib.util.find_spec("numba.cuda") is not None
+_HAS_NUMBA = False
 _HAS_NUMBA_CUDA_MLIR = importlib.util.find_spec("numba_cuda_mlir") is not None
 # Sentinel (INT64_MIN) marking a shape/stride dim resolved at runtime by libmathdx.
 _LIBMATHDX_RUNTIME = -9223372036854775808
